Interesting... The only "official" ports of Nethack are for:

     MS-DOS
     OS/2
     Macintosh
     Atari
     Amiga

There are no other officially ported versions.  Other systems (VMS, Unix,
etc.) must port their own.  So, there's no official SUN or SPARC version.  The
FAQ specifically mentions the binary versions for the personal computer
systems mentioned above, and how to obtain any of them, or the source code to
do your own port.  Somewhere, in the linc.cis.upenn.edu files, I thought I
once saw a list of computer systems that were known to have had ports done
successfully, but no official "ports" except the ones above exist.  As I'm not
a member of the NetHack officialdom, just a FAQs keeper, I have no knowledge
about why things were set up the way they were.  I can assume, though, that
ports of NetHack to Unix based systems are simple enough and the various Unix
platforms varied enought that its easier to support and manage in the form
that its in.
